Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14. Scientific reinterpretation of experiment", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"39f1c926-eea1-3747-b83f-4e9e0540e942"],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.1. Standard view", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"2f910072-7d31-4b44-965d-85055951a8af"],

Cell["Experiment measures pre-existing properties. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"1d75de01-6b0b-5f4e-9c29-21da467b0f05"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.2. RHUFT-style reinterpretation", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"d25c593b-3433-784d-a454-0ffc35239b3a"],

Cell["\<\
Experiment may instead be understood as constraining which latent field \
distinctions become stabilized in the measurement context. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"56f718d2-2466-5d4d-8a60-610cfbd80a69"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["14.3. Compatibility condition", "Subsection",ExpressionUUID->"c4ebe2a5-177b-ac41-8db7-ba7cd51d828d"],

Cell["\<\
To remain scientifically valid, this reinterpretation must recover ordinary \
laboratory predictions where current theory already succeeds.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"529ce583-efbd-c540-a4ef-5bfa03ece67f"],

Cell["\<\
Thus the new ontology must be at least empirically conservative in known \
domains. \
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"234e4f9e-022e-9143-9137-1ce456b2ae6e"],

Cell[BoxData[
 TagBox[GridBox[{
