      GrayLevel[0.8], 
      GrayLevel[0.4867756]], 
     AbsoluteThickness[1]],
   GridBoxDividers->{
    "Columns" -> {False, {True}, False}, "Rows" -> {False, {True}, False}},
   GridBoxItemSize->{"Columns" -> {{Fit}}, "Rows" -> {{Automatic}}}],
  "Grid"]], "Text", "MarkdownDelimiter",
 ShowStringCharacters->False,
 Background->None,ExpressionUUID->"548fa0d1-42df-e646-8896-ef463cf847e0"]
}, Open  ]],

Cell[CellGroupData[{

Cell["18. Immediate research tasks", "Section",ExpressionUUID->"702efab8-c9b0-7645-835f-67bf526ba67a"],

Cell["1. Define all primitive variables operationally.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b00542da-376c-4c40-b628-0f25da74dd90"],

Cell["2. Derive a proper action functional.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"52993c12-0c1d-0f42-b6c7-fb0118fd2ead"],

Cell["3. Produce Euler-Lagrange equations for the field variables.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"223eadb1-62c4-494e-b3ce-582f875d49f5"],

Cell["\<\
4. Define closure metrics on graphs, manifolds, or state spaces.\
\>", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"b189438b-fc31-ca4f-a187-85eade4fe1f4"],

Cell["5. Build spherical and toroidal node simulations.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"038e46f0-03e1-5a43-9b35-0fb63ddf974b"],

Cell["6. Compare closure-derived invariants to known constants.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"5e6b53b1-6372-3242-901f-d3bf95c133bc"],

Cell["7. Separate symbolic phenomenology from physics claims.", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6632b4ad-43a7-5647-a9f3-c77961b4c170"],

Cell["8. Build explicit falsification tests. ", "Text",ExpressionUUID->"6d0e3849-58ca-e44d-ac6b-75a6acf2c1e7"],

